  "Question": "If \\[ \\begin{aligned} &\\frac{2+3+4}{3} \\\\ &= \\frac{1990+1991+1992}{N}, \\end{aligned} \\] then \\(N = \\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3\\)",
    "B": "\\(6\\)",
    "C": "\\(1990\\)",
    "D": "\\(1991\\)",
    "E": "\\(1992\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "First evaluate the left side:\n\\[\n\\frac{2+3+4}{3}=\\frac93=3.\n\\]\nThe right numerator is \\(1990+1991+1992=5973\\). Dividing \\(5973\\) by \\(N\\) must therefore give \\(3\\), which means that \\(3\\) times \\(N\\) is \\(5973\\). Thus\n\\[\nN=5973\\div3=1991.\n\\]\nThis denominator is nonzero, and \\(5973/1991=3\\), as required. Therefore \\(\\boxed{N=1991}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
